# Optional environment for the gate pass service.
#
#   sudo cp deploy/env.example /opt/gate-pass/.env
#   sudo chown gatepass:gatepass /opt/gate-pass/.env
#   sudo chmod 600 /opt/gate-pass/.env
#   sudo systemctl restart gate-pass
#
# The service starts perfectly well WITHOUT this file — the unit references it
# with a leading "-", so a missing file is not an error. Nothing here is
# required; it exists so a setting can be changed without editing the systemd
# unit, which install.sh overwrites on every update.
#
# NEVER commit the real .env. This repository is public, and .gitignore
# excludes it.

# The key that signs session cookies. Left unset, one is generated into
# storage/secret_key (mode 600) on first run and reused for ever, which is what
# you want. Set it only to keep sessions alive across a REBUILD of the machine,
# where storage/ is not being carried over. Changing it signs everybody out.
# GATE_PASS_SECRET_KEY=

# Marks the session cookie HTTPS-only. deploy/enable-https.sh sets this once a
# certificate is actually live. Setting it by hand on a plain-HTTP site means
# the browser will not keep the cookie and nobody can sign in — the login page
# accepts the password and returns straight to itself, with no error.
# GATE_PASS_HTTPS=1

# WHERE A SECOND COPY OF THE BOOK GOES.
#
# Without this the only backup sits on the same disk as the database it is
# backing up. That protects against a mistake — a bad import, a wrong delete —
# and against nothing else: not the disk failing, not the machine being stolen,
# not the office flooding. This app deletes the source PDFs once a pass is
# issued, so the register is the ONLY copy of the book. Treat it that way.
#
# Space-separated. Each entry is either a mounted directory or anything scp
# understands. backup.sh compares sha256 after copying and fails loudly if a
# copy did not land, because a mirror nobody verified is not a mirror.
#
# A tailnet address is the useful one: it reaches the other machine wherever it
# happens to be, and the second copy should not be in the same building.
#
# GATE_PASS_BACKUP_MIRRORS="fanzart@100.123.71.31:/home/fanzart/gate-pass-backups /mnt/usb/gate-pass"
